--TEST--
A `match` written with no arms at all is `E0476`, never a panic — `nvs_types::expr`'s `Match` arm, and PHP's own answer is `UnhandledMatchError` on every evaluation
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:expressions/match
int $k = 2;
// A `match` is an expression, so an arm-less one has nothing to bind.
mixed $m = match ($k) { };
echo $m, "\n";
// The same refusal where nothing reads the value either: every path still
// throws, so there is no evaluation that does not.
match ($k) { };
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0476]: a `match` with no arms has no value
  --> %s:5:12
  |
5 | mixed $m = match ($k) { };
  |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ every path through this `match` throws
  = help: write the arm this was meant to have, or `throw` outright if the intent was to refuse every subject

error[E0476]: a `match` with no arms has no value
  --> %s:9:1
  |
9 | match ($k) { };
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ every path through this `match` throws
  = help: write the arm this was meant to have, or `throw` outright if the intent was to refuse every subject

